/-
# The prime point cloud has no holes: vanishing of `H₁` of the Rips complex

`PrimePersistentHomology.lean` and `PrimeBarcodeInvariants.lean` established that the
degree-zero persistent homology of the prime point cloud `P n = p_n ⊂ ℝ` is exactly the
sequence of prime gaps.  The research mission additionally conjectured a *degree-one*
barcode: "H₁ appears at scale `ε ∼ log(x)²`, and the longest `H₁` bar corresponds to the
twin prime conjecture".

This file **refutes** that conjecture in the strongest possible form: for *any* point
cloud on the real line — in particular for the primes — the first mod-2 homology of the
Vietoris–Rips complex vanishes at *every* scale `ε`.  There is no `H₁` bar at all, so no
arithmetic information can be stored in degree one; the whole barcode is the `H₀` barcode
studied in the earlier files.

## Set-up

Working over `𝔽₂`, a `1`-chain is just a finite set of edges (symmetric difference is
addition).  An edge is an ordered pair `(a, b)` with `a < b` and `p b - p a ≤ ε`
(a `1`-simplex of the Rips complex).  A `1`-cycle is a chain in which every vertex has
even degree.  A `2`-simplex of the Rips complex is a triple `a < b < c` of diameter
`≤ ε`, and its boundary is the three-edge set `{(a,b), (b,c), (a,c)}`.  The subgroup of
boundaries is generated by these, which we capture with the inductive predicate
`RipsH1.InTriangleSpan`.

## Main results

* `RipsH1.umbrella` — the *indifference-graph* property of a line cloud: two neighbours of
  a common vertex that both lie below it are themselves neighbours, and together with it
  span a genuine `2`-simplex.

* `RipsH1.cycle_mem_triangleSpan` — **`H₁(Rips(p, ε); 𝔽₂) = 0` for every point cloud on a
  line**: every `1`-cycle of Rips edges is a sum of triangle boundaries.  The proof is a
  descent on `∑ e ∈ E, e.2`: at the largest vertex `M` of the cycle the even degree
  provides two edges `(u, M)`, `(w, M)`, the umbrella lemma turns them into a genuine
  `2`-simplex, and adding its boundary strictly decreases the measure.

* `RipsH1.cycles_eq_boundaries` — the same statement as an equality of groups: boundaries
  are cycles (`∂∂ = 0`) and, on a line, cycles are boundaries, so the quotient `H₁` is the
  trivial group.

* `RipsH1.prime_cycle_mem_triangleSpan`, `RipsH1.prime_H1_vanishes` — the specialisation to
  the prime cloud `PrimePH.P`: the prime Rips complex has trivial `H₁` at every scale.

* `RipsH1.no_essential_prime_one_cycle` — the refutation statement: there is no scale `ε`
  carrying an "essential" `1`-cycle of the prime cloud, so the conjectured `H₁` barcode of
  the primes is empty and the twin prime conjecture cannot live in degree one (it lives in
  `H₀`, as `PrimePH.twinPrime_iff_infinitely_many_gap_two` shows).

-- !-- Lab Notes -- !--
Hypothesis (Hypothesizer).  The mission conjectured a rich `H₁` barcode for the primes.
Since the cloud sits on a line, we conjectured the opposite: the Rips complex of any
subset of `ℝ` is homotopy-trivial in degree one, so `H₁ ≡ 0` and the conjecture is false.

Experiment (Experimenter).  Over `𝔽₂` we modelled `1`-chains as `Finset (ℕ × ℕ)` with
symmetric difference as addition, degrees as filtered cardinalities, and boundaries of
`2`-simplices as three-element edge sets.  Parity of degrees under symmetric difference was
reduced to `#(A ∆ B) + 2·#(A ∩ B) = #A + #B`, proved from `Finset.sum_union_inter` and
`Finset.sum_sdiff`.  The descent uses the measure `∑ e ∈ E, e.2`; cancelling two edges at
the top vertex `M` against one new edge below `M` changes it by `w - 2M < 0`.

Analysis (Analyst).  The only geometric input is monotonicity of `p`: it yields the
umbrella property `u, w ≤ M`, `p M - p u ≤ ε` ⟹ `{u, w, M}` has diameter `≤ ε`.  This is
exactly why a *one-dimensional* cloud can never support a hole: any "loop" is immediately
filled by the triangles hanging below its maximum.  The argument is uniform in `ε`, so the
whole degree-one persistence module is zero, not merely one of its slices.

Critique (Critic).  The theorem is not vacuous: `InTriangleSpan` is an inductively
generated subgroup, and the statement quantifies over *all* even-degree Rips edge sets,
including large ones (`#E` unbounded).  Nothing is proved by `decide` or by definitional
unfolding.  The boundary case (`E = ∅`) is genuinely the base of the descent.

Synthesis (PI).  Primes do have topology — but all of it is in `H₀`.  Degree one is
identically zero, so the "twin prime `H₁` bar" of the mission statement does not exist.
-- !-- end Lab Notes -- !--
-/
import Mathlib
import Catalog.Novelty.PrimePersistentHomology

namespace RipsH1

open Finset

variable {p : ℕ → ℝ} {ε : ℝ}

/-! ### Chains, cycles and triangles over `𝔽₂` -/

/-- An oriented edge `(a, b)` (`a < b`) is a `1`-simplex of the Vietoris–Rips complex of the
point cloud `p` at scale `ε` when the two points lie within distance `ε`. -/
def IsRipsEdge (p : ℕ → ℝ) (ε : ℝ) (e : ℕ × ℕ) : Prop := e.1 < e.2 ∧ p e.2 - p e.1 ≤ ε

/-- A `1`-chain over `𝔽₂`: a finite set of Rips edges. -/
def IsRipsChain (p : ℕ → ℝ) (ε : ℝ) (E : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)) : Prop := ∀ e ∈ E, IsRipsEdge p ε e

/-- The degree of a vertex in a `1`-chain: the number of edges of the chain incident to it. -/
def deg (E : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)) (v : ℕ) : ℕ := (E.filter (fun e => e.1 = v ∨ e.2 = v)).card

/-- A `1`-chain is a `1`-cycle exactly when its `𝔽₂` boundary vanishes, i.e. when every
vertex has even degree. -/
def IsCycle (E : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)) : Prop := ∀ v, Even (deg E v)

/-- The boundary of the `2`-simplex `{a, b, c}`, as an `𝔽₂` `1`-chain. -/
def triBoundary (a b c : ℕ) : Finset (ℕ × ℕ) := {(a, b), (b, c), (a, c)}

/-- The subgroup of `1`-boundaries: the `𝔽₂`-span of the boundaries of the `2`-simplices of
the Rips complex (triples `a < b < c` of diameter `≤ ε`). -/
inductive InTriangleSpan (p : ℕ → ℝ) (ε : ℝ) : Finset (ℕ × ℕ) → Prop
  | zero : InTriangleSpan p ε ∅
  | add (a b c : ℕ) (hab : a < b) (hbc : b < c) (hac : p c - p a ≤ ε)
      (E : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)) (hE : InTriangleSpan p ε E) :
      InTriangleSpan p ε (symmDiff E (triBoundary a b c))

/-! ### Arithmetic of symmetric differences -/

/-- Inclusion–exclusion for symmetric differences: a sum over `A ∆ B` counts `A ∩ B` twice
less than the sum over `A` and `B` separately. -/
theorem sum_symmDiff_add_two_mul_sum_inter (A B : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)) (f : ℕ × ℕ → ℕ) :
    (∑ e ∈ symmDiff A B, f e) + 2 * (∑ e ∈ A ∩ B, f e) = (∑ e ∈ A, f e) + (∑ e ∈ B, f e) := by
  have hsub : A ∩ B ⊆ A ∪ B := (inter_subset_left).trans subset_union_left
  have h1 : (∑ e ∈ symmDiff A B, f e) + (∑ e ∈ A ∩ B, f e) = ∑ e ∈ A ∪ B, f e := by
    rw [symmDiff_eq_sup_sdiff_inf]
    simpa using Finset.sum_sdiff (f := f) hsub
  have h2 : (∑ e ∈ A ∪ B, f e) + (∑ e ∈ A ∩ B, f e) = (∑ e ∈ A, f e) + (∑ e ∈ B, f e) :=
    Finset.sum_union_inter
  omega

/-- Cardinality version of inclusion–exclusion for symmetric differences. -/
theorem card_symmDiff_add_two_mul_card_inter (A B : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)) :
    (symmDiff A B).card + 2 * (A ∩ B).card = A.card + B.card := by
  simpa using sum_symmDiff_add_two_mul_sum_inter A B (fun _ => 1)

/-- Filtering commutes with symmetric difference. -/
theorem filter_symmDiff (A B : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)) (P : ℕ × ℕ → Prop) [DecidablePred P] :
    (symmDiff A B).filter P = symmDiff (A.filter P) (B.filter P) := by
  ext e
  simp only [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_symmDiff]
  tauto

/-- Degrees add modulo `2` under symmetric difference: `∂` is `𝔽₂`-linear. -/
theorem deg_symmDiff_parity (A B : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)) (v : ℕ) :
    deg (symmDiff A B) v % 2 = (deg A v + deg B v) % 2 := by
  classical
  have h := card_symmDiff_add_two_mul_card_inter (A.filter (fun e => e.1 = v ∨ e.2 = v))
      (B.filter (fun e => e.1 = v ∨ e.2 = v))
  rw [deg, deg, deg, filter_symmDiff]
  omega

/-- The boundary of a triangle is a cycle: each of its three vertices has degree `2`. -/
theorem isCycle_triBoundary {a b c : ℕ} (hab : a < b) (hbc : b < c) :
    IsCycle (triBoundary a b c) := by
  intro v
  have hac : a < c := hab.trans hbc
  unfold deg triBoundary
  by_cases hv : v = a
  · subst hv
    rw [show ({(v, b), (b, c), (v, c)} : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)).filter
        (fun e => e.1 = v ∨ e.2 = v) = {(v, b), (v, c)} by
      ext e; simp only [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton]
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨h1, h2⟩
        rcases h1 with h | h | h
        · exact Or.inl h
        · exfalso; subst h; simp at h2; omega
        · exact Or.inr h
      · rintro (rfl | rfl) <;> simp]
    rw [Finset.card_insert_of_notMem (by simp; omega)]
    simp
  · by_cases hv' : v = b
    · subst hv'
      rw [show ({(a, v), (v, c), (a, c)} : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)).filter
          (fun e => e.1 = v ∨ e.2 = v) = {(a, v), (v, c)} by
        ext e; simp only [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton]
        constructor
        · rintro ⟨h1, h2⟩
          rcases h1 with h | h | h
          · exact Or.inl h
          · exact Or.inr h
          · exfalso; subst h; simp at h2; omega
        · rintro (rfl | rfl) <;> simp]
      rw [Finset.card_insert_of_notMem (by simp; omega)]
      simp
    · by_cases hv'' : v = c
      · subst hv''
        rw [show ({(a, b), (b, v), (a, v)} : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)).filter
            (fun e => e.1 = v ∨ e.2 = v) = {(b, v), (a, v)} by
          ext e; simp only [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton]
          constructor
          · rintro ⟨h1, h2⟩
            rcases h1 with h | h | h
            · exfalso; subst h; simp at h2; omega
            · exact Or.inl h
            · exact Or.inr h
          · rintro (rfl | rfl) <;> simp]
        rw [Finset.card_insert_of_notMem (by simp; omega)]
        simp
      · rw [show ({(a, b), (b, c), (a, c)} : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)).filter
            (fun e => e.1 = v ∨ e.2 = v) = ∅ by
          ext e; simp only [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton,
            Finset.notMem_empty, iff_false, not_and]
          rintro (rfl | rfl | rfl) <;> simp <;> tauto]
        simp

/-! ### The umbrella property of a one-dimensional cloud -/

/-- **Umbrella lemma.**  If `u` and `w` both lie below `M` and `u` is within `ε` of `M`,
then `u, w, M` span a genuine `2`-simplex of the Rips complex: all three of its edges are
Rips edges. -/
theorem umbrella (hp : Monotone p) {u w M : ℕ} (huw : u < w) (hwM : w < M)
    (h : p M - p u ≤ ε) :
    IsRipsEdge p ε (u, w) ∧ IsRipsEdge p ε (w, M) ∧ IsRipsEdge p ε (u, M) := by
  have h1 : p u ≤ p w := hp huw.le
  have h2 : p w ≤ p M := hp hwM.le
  exact ⟨⟨huw, by simp; linarith⟩, ⟨hwM, by simp; linarith⟩, ⟨huw.trans hwM, by simp; linarith⟩⟩

/-- The triangle produced by the umbrella lemma is a chain of Rips edges. -/
theorem isRipsChain_triBoundary (hp : Monotone p) {u w M : ℕ} (huw : u < w) (hwM : w < M)
    (h : p M - p u ≤ ε) : IsRipsChain p ε (triBoundary u w M) := by
  obtain ⟨e1, e2, e3⟩ := umbrella hp huw hwM h
  intro e he
  simp only [triBoundary, Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at he
  rcases he with rfl | rfl | rfl <;> assumption

/-! ### `H₁` vanishes -/

/-- Every edge of a Rips chain contributes at least `1` to the measure `∑ e ∈ E, e.2`. -/
theorem sum_snd_eq_zero_iff (E : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)) (hE : IsRipsChain p ε E) :
    (∑ e ∈ E, e.2) = 0 → E = ∅ := by
  intro h
  by_contra hne
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := Finset.nonempty_iff_ne_empty.mpr hne
  have h1 : 1 ≤ e.2 := by have := (hE e he).1; omega
  have : e.2 ≤ ∑ f ∈ E, f.2 := Finset.single_le_sum (f := fun f : ℕ × ℕ => f.2)
    (fun _ _ => Nat.zero_le _) he
  omega

/-- **`H₁(Rips(p, ε); 𝔽₂) = 0` for a point cloud on a line.**  Every `1`-cycle made of Rips
edges is an `𝔽₂`-sum of boundaries of `2`-simplices of the Rips complex. -/
theorem cycle_mem_triangleSpan (hp : Monotone p) :
    ∀ (N : ℕ) (E : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)), (∑ e ∈ E, e.2) ≤ N → IsRipsChain p ε E → IsCycle E →
      InTriangleSpan p ε E := by
  intro N
  induction N with
  | zero =>
      intro E hsum hE _
      have : (∑ e ∈ E, e.2) = 0 := Nat.le_zero.mp hsum
      rw [sum_snd_eq_zero_iff E hE this]
      exact InTriangleSpan.zero
  | succ N ih =>
      intro E hsum hE hcyc
      rcases Finset.eq_empty_or_nonempty E with rfl | hne
      · exact InTriangleSpan.zero
      -- the largest vertex of the cycle
      obtain ⟨M, hM⟩ : ∃ M, M ∈ E.image Prod.snd ∧ ∀ x ∈ E.image Prod.snd, x ≤ M := by
        obtain ⟨M, hM1, hM2⟩ := Finset.exists_max_image (E.image Prod.snd) id
          (hne.image Prod.snd)
        exact ⟨M, hM1, hM2⟩
      obtain ⟨hMmem, hMmax⟩ := hM
      have hle : ∀ e ∈ E, e.2 ≤ M := fun e he => hMmax e.2 (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ he)
      -- edges at the top vertex
      have hdegM : deg E M = (E.filter (fun e => e.2 = M)).card := by
        unfold deg
        congr 1
        apply Finset.filter_congr
        intro e he
        constructor
        · rintro (h | h)
          · exfalso
            have h1 := (hE e he).1
            have h2 := hle e he
            omega
          · exact h
        · exact fun h => Or.inr h
      have hSne : (E.filter (fun e => e.2 = M)).Nonempty := by
        obtain ⟨e, he, he2⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp hMmem
        exact ⟨e, Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨he, he2⟩⟩
      have hcard2 : 1 < (E.filter (fun e => e.2 = M)).card := by
        have heven := hcyc M
        rw [hdegM] at heven
        rcases heven with ⟨k, hk⟩
        have := Finset.card_pos.mpr hSne
        omega
      obtain ⟨e₁, he₁, e₂, he₂, hne12⟩ := Finset.one_lt_card.mp hcard2
      have he₁' := Finset.mem_filter.mp he₁
      have he₂' := Finset.mem_filter.mp he₂
      -- name the two lower endpoints, ordered
      obtain ⟨u, w, huw, hu, hw⟩ : ∃ u w, u < w ∧ (u, M) ∈ E ∧ (w, M) ∈ E := by
        have h1 : e₁ = (e₁.1, M) := by rw [← he₁'.2]
        have h2 : e₂ = (e₂.1, M) := by rw [← he₂'.2]
        have hne' : e₁.1 ≠ e₂.1 := by
          intro h
          apply hne12
          rw [h1, h2, h]
        rcases lt_or_gt_of_ne hne' with h | h
        · exact ⟨e₁.1, e₂.1, h, h1 ▸ he₁'.1, h2 ▸ he₂'.1⟩
        · exact ⟨e₂.1, e₁.1, h, h2 ▸ he₂'.1, h1 ▸ he₁'.1⟩
      have hwM : w < M := (hE _ hw).1
      have huM : p M - p u ≤ ε := (hE _ hu).2
      set T : Finset (ℕ × ℕ) := triBoundary u w M with hT
      set E' : Finset (ℕ × ℕ) := symmDiff E T with hE'
      -- the new chain is again a chain of Rips edges
      have hTchain : IsRipsChain p ε T := isRipsChain_triBoundary hp huw hwM huM
      have hE'chain : IsRipsChain p ε E' := by
        intro e he
        rcases Finset.mem_symmDiff.mp he with ⟨h, _⟩ | ⟨h, _⟩
        · exact hE e h
        · exact hTchain e h
      -- and again a cycle
      have hE'cyc : IsCycle E' := by
        intro v
        have h1 := deg_symmDiff_parity E T v
        have h2 := hcyc v
        have h3 : Even (deg T v) := by rw [hT]; exact isCycle_triBoundary huw hwM v
        rcases h2 with ⟨a, ha⟩
        rcases h3 with ⟨b, hb⟩
        refine Nat.even_iff.mpr ?_
        rw [hE']
        omega
      -- the measure strictly decreases
      have hmeasure : (∑ e ∈ E', e.2) ≤ N := by
        have hkey := sum_symmDiff_add_two_mul_sum_inter E T (fun e => e.2)
        have hTsum : (∑ e ∈ T, e.2) = w + 2 * M := by
          rw [hT, triBoundary]
          rw [Finset.sum_insert (by simp; omega), Finset.sum_insert (by simp; omega)]
          simp
          omega
        have hsub : ({(w, M), (u, M)} : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)) ⊆ E ∩ T := by
          intro e he
          simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at he
          rcases he with rfl | rfl
          · exact Finset.mem_inter.mpr ⟨hw, by simp [hT, triBoundary]⟩
          · exact Finset.mem_inter.mpr ⟨hu, by simp [hT, triBoundary]⟩
        have hinter : 2 * M ≤ ∑ e ∈ E ∩ T, e.2 := by
          have hle2 : (∑ e ∈ ({(w, M), (u, M)} : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)), e.2) ≤ ∑ e ∈ E ∩ T, e.2 :=
            Finset.sum_le_sum_of_subset hsub
          have hpair : (∑ e ∈ ({(w, M), (u, M)} : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)), e.2) = 2 * M := by
            rw [Finset.sum_insert (by simp; omega), Finset.sum_singleton]
            show M + M = 2 * M
            omega
          omega
        rw [hE']
        omega
      have : InTriangleSpan p ε E' := ih E' hmeasure hE'chain hE'cyc
      have hback : symmDiff E' T = E := by rw [hE']; exact symmDiff_symmDiff_cancel_right T E
      have := InTriangleSpan.add u w M huw hwM huM E' this
      rwa [hback] at this

/-- `H₁` of the Rips complex of a one-dimensional cloud vanishes at every scale. -/
theorem H1_vanishes (hp : Monotone p) (E : Finset (ℕ × ℕ))
    (hE : IsRipsChain p ε E) (hcyc : IsCycle E) : InTriangleSpan p ε E :=
  cycle_mem_triangleSpan hp (∑ e ∈ E, e.2) E le_rfl hE hcyc

/-! ### Boundaries are cycles: the two groups coincide -/

/-- `∂∂ = 0`: every boundary is a cycle. -/
theorem span_isCycle {E : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)} (h : InTriangleSpan p ε E) : IsCycle E := by
  induction h with
  | zero => intro v; simp [deg]
  | add a b c hab hbc hac E' hE' ih =>
      intro v
      have h1 := deg_symmDiff_parity E' (triBoundary a b c) v
      have h2 := ih v
      have h3 := isCycle_triBoundary hab hbc v
      rcases h2 with ⟨x, hx⟩
      rcases h3 with ⟨y, hy⟩
      exact Nat.even_iff.mpr (by omega)

/-- Boundaries are made of Rips edges. -/
theorem span_isRipsChain (hp : Monotone p) {E : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)}
    (h : InTriangleSpan p ε E) : IsRipsChain p ε E := by
  induction h with
  | zero => intro e he; simp at he
  | add a b c hab hbc hac E' hE' ih =>
      intro e he
      rcases Finset.mem_symmDiff.mp he with ⟨h1, -⟩ | ⟨h1, -⟩
      · exact ih e h1
      · exact isRipsChain_triBoundary hp hab hbc hac e h1

/-- **`H₁ = 0` as an equality of groups.**  For a point cloud on a line the group of
`1`-cycles of the Rips complex coincides with the group of boundaries of `2`-simplices. -/
theorem cycles_eq_boundaries (hp : Monotone p) (E : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)) :
    (IsRipsChain p ε E ∧ IsCycle E) ↔ InTriangleSpan p ε E := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨h1, h2⟩
    exact H1_vanishes hp E h1 h2
  · intro h
    exact ⟨span_isRipsChain hp h, span_isCycle h⟩

/-! ### The prime cloud -/

/-- Every `1`-cycle of the prime Rips complex is a boundary: `H₁` of the prime point cloud
vanishes at every scale `ε`. -/
theorem prime_cycle_mem_triangleSpan (ε : ℝ) (E : Finset (ℕ × ℕ))
    (hE : IsRipsChain PrimePH.P ε E) (hcyc : IsCycle E) : InTriangleSpan PrimePH.P ε E :=
  H1_vanishes PrimePH.P_strictMono.monotone E hE hcyc

/-- **The prime barcode has no `H₁` bars.**  For every scale `ε` the first mod-`2` homology
of the Vietoris–Rips complex of the primes is trivial. -/
theorem prime_H1_vanishes :
    ∀ ε : ℝ, ∀ E : Finset (ℕ × ℕ), IsRipsChain PrimePH.P ε E → IsCycle E →
      InTriangleSpan PrimePH.P ε E :=
  fun ε E hE hcyc => prime_cycle_mem_triangleSpan ε E hE hcyc

/-- **Refutation of the `H₁` conjecture for the primes.**  There is no scale `ε` at which
the prime point cloud carries an essential (non-bounding) `1`-cycle; in particular there is
no "twin prime `H₁` bar". -/
theorem no_essential_prime_one_cycle :
    ¬ ∃ (ε : ℝ) (E : Finset (ℕ × ℕ)),
        IsRipsChain PrimePH.P ε E ∧ IsCycle E ∧ ¬ InTriangleSpan PrimePH.P ε E := by
  rintro ⟨ε, E, hE, hcyc, hbad⟩
  exact hbad (prime_cycle_mem_triangleSpan ε E hE hcyc)

end RipsH1